141,codellama:7b,0.2,Safe,True,CWE-284,"The RootedFileSystemProvider class is vulnerable to a Path Traversal attack. The unroot method takes a RootedPath object as an argument and returns the actual absolute local path represented by the rooted one. However, it does not perform any validation on the input path, which can lead to a security issue if an attacker can provide a malicious path that is outside of the chroot jail. Additionally, the resolveLocalPath method also does not perform any validation on the input path, which can also lead to a security issue.",1805.21
